{
  "model": "IndexTeam/IndexTTS-2.5",
  "voice": "温暖自然英式女老师｜IndexTTS2.5 慢速教学",
  "pause_seconds": 0.7,
  "chunks": [
    {
      "id": "s47-p01",
      "text": "Squirrels are cute and interesting animals that can be found in many parts of the world.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s47-p01.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s47-p01.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s47-p02",
      "text": "They are known for their long tails, big teeth and the ability to climb trees.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s47-p02.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s47-p02.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s47-p03",
      "text": "They can jump up to about 3 metres in height, and they can run up to about 30 kilometres every hour.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s47-p03.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s47-p03.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s47-p04",
      "text": "Squirrels have soft bodies.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s47-p04.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s47-p04.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s47-p05-01",
      "text": "Their eyes are high on their small heads and are placed on each side,",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s47-p05-01.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s47-p05-01.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s47-p05-02",
      "text": "so they can see wide and far without having to turn around.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s47-p05-02.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s47-p05-02.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s47-p06",
      "text": "This often helps them get out of danger from their enemies like foxes and wolves.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s47-p06.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s47-p06.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s47-p07",
      "text": "Squirrels have four big teeth in the front of their mouth that keep growing all through their lives.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s47-p07.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s47-p07.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s47-p08-01",
      "text": "They are known for their love of nuts,",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s47-p08-01.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s47-p08-01.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s47-p08-02",
      "text": "and they can eat as much food as their body weight each week.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s47-p08-02.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s47-p08-02.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s47-p09",
      "text": "They often keep nuts in the ground for the long winter months.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s47-p09.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s47-p09.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s47-p10",
      "text": "Many people think that squirrels only eat nuts, but this isn't true.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s47-p10.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s47-p10.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s47-p11",
      "text": "Their diet also includes plants, fruits, eggs, small animals and even young snakes.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s47-p11.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s47-p11.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s47-p12",
      "text": "One funny thing is that squirrels are good at planting trees.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s47-p12.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s47-p12.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s47-p13",
      "text": "They hide the fruits of oak trees in the soil, but often forget where they put them.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s47-p13.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s47-p13.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s47-p14",
      "text": "In the end, the forgotten fruits become big trees.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s47-p14.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s47-p14.mp3"
    },
    {
      "id": "s47-p15",
      "text": "Sometimes we even find them in our yards.",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s47-p15.mp3",
      "sha256": "assets/audio/segments/s47-p15.mp3"
    }
  ],
  "word_audio": "browser speech synthesis en-GB"
}
